              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The funeral procession was rerouted to keep the protestors 200\u2013300 feet away from the church entrance."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Sean E. Summers (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Sean E. Summers (Petitioner), protestors displayed signs reading \u201cPriests Rape Boys,\u201d \u201cGod Hates You,\u201d and \u201cYou\u2019re Going to Hell.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Sean E. Summers (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Sean E. Summers (Petitioner), the petitioner argued that the funeral context made the protest harmful and that he was entitled to seek relief under Maryland tort law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether the First Amendment never allows a claim for intentional infliction of emotional distress unless the speech is false or true."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito also asked whether the speech was on a matter of public concern."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether the conduct was \u201coutrageous,\u201d a required element for intentional infliction of emotional distress."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56abc0c68ed7b8579ba43c6ddbbfbcd2724d83d42d38c859255948d2d9f2f841",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56abc0c68ed7-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia also questioned whether \u201cfighting words\u201d is a subjective standard."
      }
    ],
